# Chrome Web Store API v2 credentials. Copy to store/.env (gitignored).
#
# 1. CWS_PUBLISHER_ID
#    Developer Dashboard → gear icon → Account → "Publisher ID".
#
# 2. CWS_EXTENSION_ID
#    The 32-letter id of the item, visible in its dashboard URL once the item
#    exists. The first submission must be made through the dashboard, so this
#    is only available from the second release onwards.
#
# 3. CWS_CLIENT_ID / CWS_CLIENT_SECRET
#    Google Cloud Console → same Google account as the developer account:
#      a. create a project
#      b. APIs & Services → Library → enable "Chrome Web Store API"
#      c. OAuth consent screen → External → add yourself as a test user
#      d. Credentials → Create OAuth client ID → Web application
#         → Authorised redirect URI: https://developers.google.com/oauthplayground
#
# 4. CWS_REFRESH_TOKEN
#    https://developers.google.com/oauthplayground
#      → gear icon → "Use your own OAuth credentials", paste id + secret
#      → in the scope box enter: https://www.googleapis.com/auth/chromewebstore
#      → Authorize, then "Exchange authorization code for tokens"
#      → copy the refresh token
#    It does not expire unless you revoke it or leave the consent screen in
#    "Testing" mode for more than 7 days. Publish the consent screen to avoid
#    having to redo this weekly.

CWS_PUBLISHER_ID=
CWS_EXTENSION_ID=
CWS_CLIENT_ID=
CWS_CLIENT_SECRET=
CWS_REFRESH_TOKEN=
